{
  "dom_id": "step-71612",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Determining Whether a Square Root Is a Real Number",
  "problem": "Which of the following square roots are real numbers?\n\nI. $\\sqrt{0}$\n\nII. $\\sqrt{1.5}$\n\nIII. $\\sqrt{-4}$",
  "worked_solution": "The square root of a negative number is not a real number, while the square root of a non-negative number is a real number.\n\nLet's look at each square root in turn.\n\n- $\\sqrt{0}$ is the square root of $0,$ which is a non-negative number. So $\\sqrt{0}$ is a real number. In fact, since $0 = 0^2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{0} = \\sqrt{0^2} = 0.\n$$\n\n- $\\sqrt{1.5}$ is the square root of $1.5,$ which is a non-negative number. So $\\sqrt{1.5}$ is a real number.\n\n- $\\sqrt{-4}$ is the square root of $-4,$ which is a negative number. So $\\sqrt{-4}$ is not a real number.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only\".",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
